  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Harin Kumar Hp vs Union Of India on 4 December, 2024 Author: Hemant Chandangoudar Bench: Hemant Chandangoudar -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:50001 Wp No. 8277 of 2024 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 4Th Day Of December, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr Justice Hemant Chandangoudar Writ Petition No. 8277 Of 2024 (Gm-Ten) Between: Harin Kumar Hp S/O Puttaswamy Gowda, Aged About 34 Years, Proprietor Of M/S Cafelicious, A Proprietorship Firm, Having Its Registred Office At No 93/91 D Block, 1St Main, 1St Cross, Belavatha Village, Mysuru 570 003. ...Petitioner (By Sri. Divyathej A B., Advocate) AND: 1. UNION OF INDIA DEPARTMENT OF POSTS, DAK BHAWAN, NEW DELHI 11000 REPRESENTED BY ITS SECRETARY. Digitally signed by B K MAHENDRAKUMAR 2. CHIEF POSTMASTER GENERAL KARNATAKA CIRCLE Location: HIGH COURT OF PALACE ROAD, BENGALURU 560001 KARNATAKA REPRESENTED BY MR RAJENDRA KUMAR. 3. POST MASTER GENERAL KARNATAKA CIRCLE, PALACE ROAD, BENGALURU 560001 REPRESENTED BY MR L K DASH. Harin Kumar Hp vs Union Of India on 4 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/149610276/ 1 4. THE DIRECTOR POSTAL TRAINING CENTRE POSTAL TRAINING CENTRE, NAZARBAD MYSURU 570010 REPRESENTED BY MR ASHISH SINGH TAKUR. -2- NC: 2024:KHC:50001 WP No. 8277 of 2024 5. ASSISTANT DIRECTOR (ADMIN) POSTAL TRAINING CENTRE, NAZARBAD MYSURU 570010 REPRESENTED BY MR C PRAKASH. 6. TENDER TECHNICAL AND FINANCIAL EVALUATION COMMITTEE MEMBERS POSTAL TRAINING CENTRE, NAZARBAD MYSURU 570 010 REPRESENTED BY MR K V L N MURTHY. 7. MR ASHISH SINGH TAKUR S/O NOT KNOWN TO THE PETITIONER AGED MAJOR, WORKING AT THE POSTAL TRAINING CENTRE, NAZARBAD MYSURU 570010. 8. MR K V L N MURTHY S/O NOT KNOWN TO THE PETITIONER AGED MAJOR, WORKING AT THE POSTAL TRAINING CENTRE, NAZARBAD MYSURU 570010. 9. MS. K STAR FOOD & HOSPITALITY SERVICES 12/104, MRIDULA, VASANTH CULA COMPLEX GHODBUNDER ROAD, WAGHBILL THANE (WEST)-4000615. ...RESPONDENTS (BY SRI. H SHANTHI BHUSHAN., ADVOCATE FOR R1 TO R8; SRI. K PRASANNA SHETTY, ADVOCATE FOR R9) THIS WRIT PETITION IS FILED UNDER ARTICLES 226 AND 227 OF THE CONSTITUTION OF INDIA PRAYING TO QUASH THE TENDER NOTIFICATION DATED 22/12/2023 BEARING BID NO.GEM/2023/B/4168766 PASSED BY THE R5 DATED (PRODUCED AS ANNEXURE-A) AND ETC. THIS PETITION, COMING ON FOR PRELIMINARY HEARING IN 'B' GROUP, THIS DAY, ORDER WAS MADE THEREIN AS UNDER: Harin Kumar Hp vs Union Of India on 4 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/149610276/ 2 CORAM: HON'BLE MR JUSTICE HEMANT CHANDANGOUDAR -3- NC: 2024:KHC:50001 WP No. 8277 of 2024 ORAL ORDER",
    "facts": "The respondent No.5 issued a tender notification dated 22.12.2023 inviting bids for providing canteen services for a period of one year. In response to the tender document, the petitioner, respondent No.9, and 23 other bidders submitted their bids. The technical bid of the petitioner was rejected by respondent No.6, citing non-compliance with Clause 3(vii) of the Additional Terms and Conditions. 5. Clause 3(vii) of the Additional Terms and Conditions stipulates that the bidder must furnish an FSSAI license covering the seven products listed therein. Additionally, the successful bidder must produce an FSSAI certificate from the local office within fifteen days to continue operating the canteen at PTC Mysuru. 6. In the present case, the petitioner submitted an FSSAI license for only one product, not for all seven products as required by Clause 3(vii). Therefore, the rejection of the petitioner's technical bid is in conformity with the Additional Terms and Conditions of the tender document. The contract awarded to respondent No.9 is also consistent with the tender document's requirements.",
    "arguments": "However, the petitioner submitted a license for only one product and, therefore, did not satisfy the requirement."
  },
